{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/qwen_proxy_validation/transcript-merge-regression/workspace/reports/incidents/transcript-merge.md << 'EOF'\n# Transcript Merge Incident Note\n\n## Root Cause\n\n## Summary\n\nThe reducer in \"'`replay/merge.py` incorrectly grouped tool_output events by\n`(role, tool_name)` instead of using `event_id` for stable identity. This caused\ndistinct tool outputs with the same tool name to be merged into a single block.\n\nAdditionally, debug_only fragments after `response.completed` were not being\nfiltered during the merge phase, causing them to appear in rendered output.\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n1. **Stable identity**: `_event_key()` now uses `event_id` for all events,\n   ensuring distinct tool outputs remain distinct even when sharing the same\n   tool name.\n\n2. **Post-completion filtering**: `merge_records()` now filters out\n   `debug_only` events after `response.completed` during the merge phase,\n   not just at render time.\n\n3. **Summary source**: `incident_summary.py` now counts directly from merged\n   events instead of rendered lines, using `count_source: \"merged_events\"`.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun: `python3 -m unittest tests.test_merge tests.test_render tests.test_incident_summary`\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
